00:12:09.555 --> 00:12:11.715
that's available through ArcGIS Online.

00:12:12.435 --> 00:12:23.490
So when we were looking at the satellite imagery, what we're looking for is dark spots. And then if these dark spots have other indications that it could be water. So the branching patterns that you can kind of see in the figure on the left

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:26.210
are good indications that that's water flowing,

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:37.825
