00:12:39.265 --> 00:13:01.715
So once you kind of establish this might be a potential vernal pool, then we use Google Earth imagery in tandem with that to kind of see, okay, is something consistently there from looking at other years? So you can see that in spring of two thousand and eight, it was also present. So that's a good indication that something is going on there. And then also double checking that it is seasonal because again, vernal pools are seasonal habitat.

00:13:01.955 --> 00:13:06.035
So if it is filled year round, then it's not going to be considered a vernal pool.

00:13:06.595 --> 00:13:13.650
